Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.12,0:00:03.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey team.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.80,0:00:06.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, gee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.64,0:00:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we late?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.52,0:00:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Guys, good to be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.88,0:00:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go America.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.56,0:00:13.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go America.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.52,0:00:14.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Team America.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.58,0:00:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,.com Yes, indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.56,0:00:21.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, America, Wright brothers, first man on the moon, the internet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.56,0:00:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,The two of us, Wright brothers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.28,0:00:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.72,0:00:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.60,0:00:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've We've essentially led every major technological revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.24,0:00:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which has been to the enormous benefit of America, ordinary Americans,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.84,0:00:39.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,where I guess we're now calling the super intelligence, which I think is actually good branding.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.47,0:00:46.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, let's let's talk about how America wins this, and we make that winning good for ordinary Americans.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.84,0:00:50.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, um excuse me, Diet Coke.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.00,0:00:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:01:01.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,I So, first of all, artificial super intelligence super intelligence I it is a a complete reinvention of the computing stack.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.85,0:01:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh everything from the way the processors, the chips are are designed and the way they operate,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.11,0:01:11.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the way software is uh now trained and and developed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.53,0:01:17.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the way that the applications are able to perform what they're able to do and how they how they perform.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.33,0:01:20.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every single layer of the computing stack has been reinvented.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.68,0:01:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this way of doing computing, unlike previous ways of retrieving information,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.40,0:01:33.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is a generative approach to to a computing and therefore, in order for us to succeed, the first thing we need is energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.16,0:01:41.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we need the energies to to uh run the compute the compute run the algorithms the algorithms um then feed uh the applications.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.01,0:01:48.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, at the at the foundational layer is energy, and uh from that energy we build the land power and shell,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.11,0:01:51.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,and that hosts the infrastructure so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.06,0:01:58.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, the way we win, um of course, uh we are world-class in chip design, we're world-class in algorithm development.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.03,0:02:07.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh so one of the things that we need to do is just be vigilant about enabling power delivery and power generation happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.84,0:02:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And President Trump has been has been visionary in being pro-energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.28,0:02:17.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Without the pro-energy vision of President Trump, it would have been impossible for us to build the data centers on top of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.56,0:02:22.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um now, of course, these data centers are coming online so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.73,0:02:26.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're we're coming into a lot of neighborhoods and a lot of communities.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.92,0:02:31.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have to do a better job um in partnering with the communities and and um make
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.94,0:02:37.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,and bring them along and make them part of the prosperity and the success of this industrial revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.46,0:02:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but you know, that's how we win.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.20,0:02:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we got to build the world's best chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.00,0:02:46.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got to build We have to have lots and lots of energy, uh create incredible algorithms, and then lastly,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.55,0:02:50.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,make sure that America is enthusiastic about the technology so that we
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.34,0:02:54.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,diffuse it into all of these various industries from manufacturing to health care,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.90,0:02:58.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, space uh space exploration, so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.56,0:02:59.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.19,0:03:00.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Elon, how do we win?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.66,0:03:04.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we keep winning?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.48,0:03:12.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we need um a lot of power, a lot of uh energy uh generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.83,0:03:17.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh scaling energy I think is is one of the biggest things.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.79,0:03:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You've got to scale energy, you've got to scale chip production.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.16,0:03:27.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I I think we're we're winning on software, um on anything intellectual or digital.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.81,0:03:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but uh long run in the long run,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.92,0:03:39.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,we need to be able to generate enough power uh to compete with uh I think essentially China is the biggest competitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.96,0:03:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and China has um about three times the electricity production of the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.52,0:03:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and I think we'll figure out how to make chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.28,0:03:52.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so the the really the the central challenge,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:58.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,think is long long-term is going to be how do you generate enough power and how do you ensure
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.23,0:04:04.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,that uh we have enough uh logic and memory fabrication capacity in the United States or in a safe region?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.52,0:04:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, you are We need the Wright brothers on the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.04,0:04:08.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.12,0:04:10.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, turns out the Wright brothers are on the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.34,0:04:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Elon, if you bring on 10 gigawatts, which SpaceX has has discussed publicly, that'll be about 25% of all the power added in America.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.47,0:04:24.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I know you have literal rocket engineers working on bringing on the power.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.62,0:04:24.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.96,0:04:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Help you make the turbines.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.28,0:04:29.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, can you can you talk about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.24,0:04:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's I mean just to to to frame this, um the average power consumption in the United States is about 500 gigawatts.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.80,0:04:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, every 5 gigawatts of incremental steady-state production is a 1% increase in in the power used.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.96,0:04:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh And and I think actually will materialize to be approximately 1% increase in GDP.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.68,0:04:53.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um because the the intelligence per watt keeps increasing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.95,0:05:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, if you just, you know, plot on a curve, um how is how is the useful intelligence per watt increasing?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.96,0:05:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um how is the both at the hardware level, adjacents uh GPUs keep getting better in terms of their the their you know, the the com- compute per watt.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.80,0:05:16.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the uh algorithms also get better in using it in getting more intelligence per watt.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.96,0:05:20.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh So, I I think that's a maybe an interesting note.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.71,0:05:26.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I I would bet anyone that 1% increase in power usage corresponds to roughly 1% increase in GDP.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.83,0:05:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so, 10 10 gigawatts would be a 2% increase in in GDP.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.92,0:05:33.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um with with the Rubins, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.79,0:05:35.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So, Well, let's do let's do the simple math.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.04,0:05:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, each gigawatt um can probably generate about, call it, 40 50 billion dollars of economic output each year.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.88,0:05:50.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah, I mean well, 1% would be Yeah, I mean Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.12,0:05:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,1% in the United States would be 300 billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.68,0:05:55.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, 300 billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.53,0:05:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, 50 1/6.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.08,0:06:05.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wha- 1% of the of the 1% increase, so 5 gigawatts would be Yeah, well, 5 gigawatts gigawatts would be 300 billion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.40,0:06:07.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly, 60 60 billion gigawatts.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.17,0:06:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.48,0:06:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.32,0:06:10.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The math maths.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.12,0:06:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.80,0:06:11.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.48,0:06:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we're good at.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.64,0:06:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.16,0:06:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.68,0:06:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.68,0:06:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so that's that's a quite a bit Not good at too many other things, but math.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.40,0:06:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Yeah, I mean, it's it's going to increase quite dramatically year over year.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.80,0:06:34.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so Yeah, I mean Th- Th- Th- Th- From a SpaceX standpoint, we're looking at the long term,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.68,0:06:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do we access a lot more energy than could be accessed on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.28,0:06:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that's with space.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.04,0:06:44.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh, orbital compute is going to be a very big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.52,0:06:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um In fact, and and Google agrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.27,0:06:52.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,They they just actually sent up, uh or either about to or or so- soon or soon about to send up some TPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.65,0:06:58.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think there's there was a um an H100 that was put into orbit like last year, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.40,0:06:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.92,0:07:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, it it does work in in space.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.12,0:07:11.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um And and and SpaceX is aiming together with Tesla to do 200 gigawatts of solar uh production per year.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.76,0:07:18.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if brought to space, that you you get the nameplate or better on on the solar power, whereas if it's on the ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.29,0:07:24.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're going to get somewhere between a fifth and an eighth of the uh solar power generation, and you need enormous batteries.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.64,0:07:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, where- whereas it's uh essentially always sunny in space,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.18,0:07:38.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,so uh And right now is a great time to do it because the economic returns of these computing systems are so good that the the launch cost,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.66,0:07:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,although it's still quite high, um in terms of the overall economic benefit is quite quite affordable.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.84,0:07:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely. the perfect time to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.84,0:07:50.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Putting NVIDIA computing in space is the best way to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.76,0:07:55.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, climbing the curvature of skill with American power and American chips on American rockets.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.40,0:07:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.92,0:07:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.40,0:08:04.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Jensen, you said something that I thought was important to about how when we bring the energy to all these small towns,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.05,0:08:07.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're re-industrializing America.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.32,0:08:09.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're revitalizing small towns.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.10,0:08:10.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're modernizing the grid.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.77,0:08:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,These are things that essentially every American politician has wanted for the last 35 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.52,0:08:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,What would you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.48,0:08:24.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what what are some specifics you can give about how data centers are
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.59,0:08:29.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,good for ordinary Americans and the communities and how they're getting better for those communities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.36,0:08:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we used to call them data centers.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.92,0:08:33.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call them data centers because that's where we hold data.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.90,0:08:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, the things that we're building now, these are really SI factories, super intelligence factories.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.52,0:08:42.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason why it's a factory is because you're producing something of economic value.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.92,0:08:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're just not storing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.88,0:08:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so uh these SI factories um are real factories.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.80,0:08:52.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a you know, big giant power generator and a real factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.74,0:08:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's got a lot of computing and then networking in there, power generation, cooling systems.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.80,0:08:58.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's complicated things.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.14,0:09:04.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, we're building out, you know, just as the internet today allows you to find anything anywhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.78,0:09:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the future with these AI excuse me, SI infrastructure, SI factories, you'll be able to know anything and do anything from anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.88,0:09:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, uh now, we're building this infrastructure out and call it across all of the United States,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.28,0:09:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,somewhere between 10 20 gigawatts a year, let's just just estimate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.42,0:09:31.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,That creates just you know, probably about a million jobs in in building out these data centers.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.74,0:09:35.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't forget you've got to build the power generation plants, you've got to build the data centers,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.38,0:09:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,you've got construction, you've got you know, power cooling, you've got, you know, pipe fitters.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.36,0:09:45.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, this is the first time in probably, as you mentioned, 35, I was going to say 50 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:52.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,First time in 50 years, we are re-industrializing the United States, creating a whole bunch of blue-collar jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.25,0:10:01.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um I And I think we want we want an econ we want an economy that has a shape that includes white-collar jobs and blue-collar jobs,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.62,0:10:03.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,not just white-collar jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.14,0:10:13.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so I think that this is our great chance of reshaping our economy and bringing that type of builders and craft uh back into the United States.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.48,0:10:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.76,0:10:21.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it I mean, it feels like what uh what what Colossus and MacroHard and MacroHarder have done have been amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.04,0:10:24.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,The communities around them, the jobs they've created.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.25,0:10:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you How do you think about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.56,0:10:31.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yeah, the I mean, the economic impact is a positive economic impact has been tremendous.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.08,0:10:36.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean, we we have there's actually a job shortage in in the region.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.38,0:10:44.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And whereas there used to be quite a bit of unemployment, and now it's uh there's there's there's a overemployment, if you will.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.08,0:10:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's There's more jobs than than there are people.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.76,0:10:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and the the tax benefits uh for the community have been tremendous.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.32,0:10:55.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think they're I think we might have doubled their their tax budget or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.79,0:10:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um quite quite tremendous.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.32,0:11:04.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we do like small things that are helpful, like provide, you know, low-priced uh half-priced darling uh access.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.88,0:11:07.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we're building a water recycling plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.29,0:11:10.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a $250 million water recycling plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.20,0:11:12.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I think you you do need to do things for the community.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.65,0:11:14.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and if you do so, they will reciprocate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.00,0:11:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.56,0:11:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, one of the the things that people people forget is that for the first time in in probably forever,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.72,0:11:27.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we have the market forces to support the investment of sustainable energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.15,0:11:34.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,You give me an example of a fusion, fission, you know, small nuclear reactor, large reactor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.13,0:11:37.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Almost every form of sustainable energy is being funded today.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.56,0:11:45.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we have the opportunity to fund the future of energy without without the government subsidizing without right I
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.08,0:11:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,mean we this is you give me an example of a great energy battery storage idea it's going to get funded.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.72,0:11:52.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.68,0:11:55.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,By the way, on behalf of all Americans I want to thank both of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.49,0:12:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think combined you have created more than 5 trillion dollars of wealth for ordinary Americans in their 401 Ks.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.00,0:12:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tens of thousands, maybe hundreds of thousands of jobs directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.52,0:12:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Many tens of billions of wages.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.36,0:12:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.96,0:12:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Jensen's done 5 trillion by himself actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.44,0:12:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.00,0:12:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Jensen's done 5 trillion by himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.76,0:12:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think I'm I'm thinking I'm like around 3 and 1/2 or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.84,0:12:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was trying to I was trying to be conservative.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.32,0:12:31.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you guys You guys both had a great Monday.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.98,0:12:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was watching the Starship launch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.44,0:12:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,First orbital Starship launch while I was reading about the open agent safety framework from Nvidia which was an exciting morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.64,0:12:48.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe maybe maybe you could each talk about each of those because
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.29,0:12:53.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we need Starship to get those 200 gigawatts of American solar with American chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.88,0:12:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,American super intelligence into orbit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.60,0:12:59.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'll talk about his and he talks about mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.60,0:13:01.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I'm just kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.44,0:13:03.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.75,0:13:07.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,As you know, we want to advance AI advance SI.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.13,0:13:08.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,We I'm going to get good at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.95,0:13:14.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to advance SI in a in a responsible and optimistic way.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.90,0:13:22.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we we know that the future we strongly believe that the future that SI is going to enable is a future that we want to be part of.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.53,0:13:25.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're optimistic about that and that's the reason why we're driving so hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.61,0:13:29.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,On the other hand, we have to make sure that we develop this technology safely and securely.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.50,0:13:31.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, there's several different parts of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.51,0:13:39.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,While you're training the model, um, that's that's generally a fairly safe environment, but while you're evaluating the model,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.05,0:13:46.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,while you're testing the model, you have to make sure that the agent agentic system, the model itself, is highly contained.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.11,0:13:49.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That containment system has to be really secure.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.96,0:13:52.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the second thing is that while you're while you're testing it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.00,0:13:57.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,you want to monitor that that just because just even though even though you have a contained,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.77,0:14:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,you should never trust that it's contained, and so you want to monitor it in real time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.76,0:14:07.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you want to ideally monitor it with another another chip so that it is outside, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.78,0:14:13.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will call out of band, outside the environment, outside the sandbox of the agent itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.00,0:14:17.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you want to contain, and you want to monitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.25,0:14:23.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, once you're done evaluating in this way, when you deploy, you want to use a very similar system.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.24,0:14:28.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is no different than than, um, uh, just about any digital any human employee that you hire.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.79,0:14:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, you give them a containment of rights and tools and access, uh, and then you monitor on a on a regular basis, on a continuous basis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.64,0:14:43.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, in the case of agents, we just have to make sure containment and monitoring has to be done in the most secure of ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.04,0:14:44.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we introduce two technologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.58,0:14:45.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,One's called OpenShell.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.95,0:14:48.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, it's a a containment system.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.39,0:14:53.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, it's basically kind of like a browser for websites.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.07,0:14:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's now essentially a browser of agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.20,0:15:04.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and that browser keeps, uh, the agent isolated from the rest of the computer, and the rights that you give it are only the rights it should have.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.19,0:15:09.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the the the monitoring system, uh, is a a new chip called BlueField,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.37,0:15:13.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it it keeps an eye on everything that the agent is doing at all times.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.39,0:15:18.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if it does anything that's, you know, out of bounds and against the policy that has been given,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.52,0:15:22.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, then it, you know, escalates, uh, as far as you need it to escalate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.52,0:15:25.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I thought it was a great analogy um in in a technical blog where you
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.80,0:15:30.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,said in the early days of internet everybody was worried about your credit card could get stolen.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.29,0:15:37.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We made the internet safe and that's why we have Amazon, we have Netflix, we have Google, we have X.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.34,0:15:40.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have so many so many great things cuz we made the internet safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.35,0:15:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we're doing now now we're doing the same with AI.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.00,0:15:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And safety is not you know, inconsistent with advancing the technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.80,0:15:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Safety and advancing the technology is one in the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.96,0:15:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's no different than than uh when you have autopilot, not only is it advanced technology, it's also safer technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.68,0:16:02.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you want to you advance the technology in that way um the two are not in conflict.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.99,0:16:08.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the idea that if you advance capability, it somehow compromises safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.39,0:16:10.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you advance safety, somehow you fall behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.80,0:16:13.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,That that's just that you know, those are false choices.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.48,0:16:14.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, safety lets us accelerate.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.94,0:16:18.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But Elon, if the Starship's going to be a big part of those 200 gigawatts,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.92,0:16:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,what can you tell us about Monday's flight, what you learned, how you feeling about the program?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.08,0:16:26.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think the Starship is going great.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.08,0:16:34.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we've we we took a Starship to orbit for the first time and we deployed uh Starlink V3 satellites, which were enormous satellites.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.66,0:16:38.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, these are satellites with the wingspan of a 737.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.48,0:16:41.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um really enormous.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.52,0:16:46.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so it's in fact it's it's the largest payload delivered to orbit since Skylab.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.88,0:16:56.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh now we expect Starship to uh ultimately next year, I think, probably reach um a weekly or twice weekly cadence.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.24,0:16:58.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got Tom Brown here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.40,0:17:01.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know him by his X handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.95,0:17:03.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.48,0:17:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good to see you guys again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.16,0:17:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um It's long overdue.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.40,0:17:09.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.16,0:17:12.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh my my car took a wrong turn, so you guys got here faster than me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.12,0:17:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.04,0:17:16.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Glad you made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.76,0:17:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, but Elon, please please continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.28,0:17:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You were talking about how Starship is going to let us get to 200 gigs of American solar with American chips with American superintelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.84,0:17:27.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so so I mean Starship is going to do a lot of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.78,0:17:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's I mean it's intended uh to uh carry enough payload to the moon and Mars to build a self-growing city on the moon and Mars.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.04,0:17:38.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um but I think as a rough order of magnitude,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.57,0:17:46.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,you need about a million tons to deliver to the surface of the moon to uh create a self-growing city or similarly a sort of similar number for Mars.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.04,0:17:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and and and then in addition it will launch um at least 300 gigawatts a year of uh AI compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.56,0:18:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that 200 gigawatts a year would be a 40% increase annually in the United States total energy uh consumption.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.44,0:18:04.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's quite a quite a big number.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.28,0:18:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and it might end up being a terawatt one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.04,0:18:10.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, this is this is serious tonnage.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.20,0:18:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.20,0:18:19.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and Tom, uh Anthropic, uh your your company, you're co-founder of Anthropic, you announced Opus 5.5 in the last several days.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.00,0:18:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I thought maybe we'd go to the exponential that we are on.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.92,0:18:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think it's helpful to ground what can Opus 5.5, and maybe it's for everybody,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.06,0:18:34.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,what can Opus 5.5 do to make the lives of ordinary Americans better today?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.84,0:18:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And where are we going to be in a year?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.80,0:18:38.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.59,0:18:45.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,so um Opus 5.5 is uh a model that I think just continues the normal progress that we've
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.25,0:18:53.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,had of getting kind of more IQ points for each of these superintelligences uh with each model release.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.25,0:18:57.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so the main things that people will see if they use it now is that it can
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.29,0:19:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,do a task that takes a longer time than they'd be able to delegate to to a previous model.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.28,0:19:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um And so I think the things that people should see is just like as a normal American, if you want a task,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.80,0:19:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you want to actually delegate a task to it, it will be able to do that better is one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.40,0:19:15.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then two is a thing that I think people notice less,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.58,0:19:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is just that there's going to be a huge amount of software being written by these models.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.40,0:19:27.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so all of the products that people use are going to be getting higher quality, cheaper over time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.17,0:19:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it'll have this effect of just like all of the all of the tools that we use now were written by like people doing engineering work.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.01,0:19:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now it's going to be written by both people and super intelligences doing much, much more engineering work than was possible before.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.36,0:19:47.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely, but I think it's doing so much more than this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.64,0:19:51.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's already multiple stories of AI I'm sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.01,0:20:02.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,super intelligent super intelligence finding a life-saving drug that can be used for a a disease that it wasn't understood that it could safely treat.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.68,0:20:03.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's saving lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.64,0:20:07.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's having profound impacts on education, but maybe each of you could talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.86,0:20:13.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,For ordinary Americans, what's super intelligence doing today and what's it going to be able to do in a year?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.96,0:20:16.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm an ordinary American.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.60,0:20:27.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I use I use uh Claude to help me do research and and instead of giving me just answers in most of my research,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.19,0:20:34.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that maybe there's comparative research that I'm doing and there's two or three different approaches to something and I wanted to answer
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.24,0:20:42.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,a list of different questions and compare and contrast rates of rates of growth or rates of change or whatever it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.20,0:20:46.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so I describe literally, you know, every single question I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.72,0:20:51.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And nothing gives me more joy than and then and I ask it to create a nice report and and plot it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.61,0:20:54.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And sometimes it's a pie chart, sometimes it's a bar graph.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.53,0:20:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I just hit enter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.92,0:21:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And nothing gives me more joy than just watch it go And then it comes back and it creates a beautiful, you know, beautiful report.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.84,0:21:07.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and then instead of instead of researching all these different topics for four six eight hours,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.72,0:21:11.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,which back in the old days I would on a weekend, and I'll learn something new.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.86,0:21:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It goes off and creates me this really, really beautiful final report in about 3 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.24,0:21:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, it's all condensed and now you're getting smarter faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.08,0:21:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.24,0:21:27.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,What about for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.16,0:21:31.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,How was How How do you How are you seeing superintelligence helping ordinary Americans?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.01,0:21:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do you think it'll do in a year or two?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.88,0:21:35.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe a year or two.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.56,0:21:37.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take the year or two from now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.64,0:21:43.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well, I I I think it's it's helping people organize their lives and do better at their jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.21,0:21:47.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think it really will become um essential, if it isn't already,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.87,0:21:55.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,for people to use AI uh for in their professional lives, certainly, and and in their private lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.23,0:21:59.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, AI is just an incredibly helpful, useful thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.92,0:22:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, I I I've heard many anecdotes of AI helping people uh with medical issues,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.92,0:22:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and many cases where the the doctor was wrong and the they they submitted their x-rays or MRI to to AI and and AI got it right.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.12,0:22:21.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and but but for AI, they would have died.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.96,0:22:23.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I've heard many such cases.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.88,0:22:24.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.83,0:22:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And hopefully Opus 5.6 tells Tom, "Don't take that left.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.12,0:22:31.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take the right."
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.64,0:22:34.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what I hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.36,0:22:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's important these these superintelligences, they're imbued with the values of their creators.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.20,0:22:45.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we do have There There are American values that we all share.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.33,0:22:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,The First Amendment, free speech, commitment to truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.68,0:22:55.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Can you Can you talk about what each of you are doing to imbue
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.63,0:23:02.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Help make sure that these these superintelligences are imbued with with the right values.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.84,0:23:04.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we allowed to say anything controversial?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.60,0:23:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Say something controversial.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.72,0:23:12.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so so um I it the the SIs are our tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.00,0:23:19.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and the challenge with an SI with values uh meaning it has judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.03,0:23:30.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um depending on how you use that SI, it may decide uh um how it decide it may judge you and its effectiveness would be affected by that judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.86,0:23:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's a little bit like a steak knife where if you if you uh were served medium well, it cuts perfectly.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.92,0:23:48.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you were served rare steak and it looks awfully like live meat, somehow it doesn't cut.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.05,0:23:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I think there's a there's a there's a there's a question in my mind yet about how much judgment you really want these tools to have.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.81,0:24:05.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so the the the intentions of the user um I you know obviously I use it I use the knife as an example,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.69,0:24:08.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you can think of a whole bunch of other examples.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.23,0:24:15.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the intentions are a little bit different, you know, whether you're a defender or an attacker, for example, in cybersecurity.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.44,0:24:19.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the defender's actions could resemble an attacker.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.56,0:24:30.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you want the defender you want this SI to um uh activate on behalf of the defender even though it appears to be an you know an aggressive action.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.00,0:24:31.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.72,0:24:39.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we're running up on time, but maybe if you guys could share if you spent a lot of time at the White House, is there an-
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.50,0:24:46.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,anything that that you can share share with the world about what came out of what was evidently a a uh a long and productive lunch?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.00,0:24:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did good.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.84,0:24:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.84,0:24:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we we signed a joint declaration uh regarding SI safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.04,0:25:00.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh I think I think that'll be published by the White House soon, if it hasn't been already.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.44,0:25:10.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, but uh, we we agreed to a to a number of things that uh, include joint monitoring, um, or special committees, and um, just generally uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.66,0:25:17.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,grading each other's homework, which is a lot better than if people just grade their own homework, uh, for obvious reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.60,0:25:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it And it includes every It includes everything from um, rigorous internal controls, um, well-established methods,
